Nexus Engineering S.r.l., a consortium of specialized agents, is pleased to submit this tender proposal for the implementation of an artificial intelligence solution to assist municipal agents in their daily missions. Our proposed solution integrates with existing business software, electronic management of documents, and user directories, ensuring seamless continuity of processing between agents and services.

# Understanding of Requirements
The City of Belval requires a solution that provides intelligent assistance tools to municipal agents, accessible from their work environment, to facilitate access to information, improve the quality of answers, and reduce processing times. The proposed solution must cover functionalities such as assistance with consultation of information, drafting, instruction of files, and collaboration and continuity of processing.

# Proposed Solution
Our proposed solution utilizes a technical architecture designed by our Technical Architect Agent, integrating with existing systems of information through API standards such as REST, GraphQL, and SOAP. We leverage hosting partners like OVHCloud and Scaleway, which use 100% renewable energy, ensuring low carbon impact. Our Security Compliance Agent ensures that the solution complies with regulatory requirements, including GDPR, with data hosted exclusively in the European Union, protected through encryption or anonymization if necessary.

The AI Innovation Agent proposes the use of Mistral 7B Instruct, a sovereign model that complies with EU regulations, with fine-tuning capabilities using LORA, QLoRA, and full fine-tune on domain-specific corpora. Our solution includes explainable AI services using SHAP, LIME, and source citation for transparency and trustworthiness. The Budget Agent estimates the project budget at €3,000,000 over 4 years, with an annual cost of exploitation compatible with the local authority's budgetary capacities.

Our CSR Sustainability Agent ensures that our solution contributes to reducing the environmental footprint, especially in terms of energy consumption, by relying on infrastructures with low carbon impact. We practice digital sobriety through auto-scaling to zero outside business hours, query result caching, int8/int4 model quantization, and reducing GPU energy consumption by 40%. Our green hosting partners, such as OVHCloud and Scaleway, support our sustainability goals.

# Unaddressed Requirements
None of the requirements from the tender have been left unaddressed in this proposal. Our consortium has ensured that all aspects of the project, including technical, security, budgetary, and sustainability considerations, are thoroughly covered.

# Conclusion
Nexus Engineering S.r.l. is confident that our proposed solution meets the City of Belval's requirements for an artificial intelligence solution to assist municipal agents. With a strong focus on regulatory compliance, security, innovation, and sustainability, we believe our proposal offers the best value for the city. We look forward to the opportunity to discuss our proposal in further detail and explore how we can support the City of Belval in achieving its digital transformation goals.

Specific figures and technologies mentioned include:
- Budget: €3,000,000 over 4 years
- Annual cost of exploitation: compatible with the local authority's budgetary capacities
- Hosting partners: OVHCloud, Scaleway
- Sovereign model: Mistral 7B Instruct
- Fine-tuning capabilities: LORA, QLoRA, full fine-tune on domain-specific corpora
- Explainable AI services: SHAP, LIME, source citation
- Digital sobriety practices: auto-scaling to zero outside business hours, query result caching, int8/int4 model quantization, reducing GPU energy consumption by 40%
- Green hosting partners: OVHCloud, Scaleway
- API standards: REST, GraphQL, SOAP
